  "notes": "To divide something into parts, typically in a deliberate or systematic manner. Commonly used in financial, legal, and technical contexts such as splitting payments, partitioning land, or dividing data.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}{払|ばら}い: installment payment\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}{統治|とうち}: divide and rule\n- {均等|きんとう}に{分割|ぶんかつ}する: to divide equally\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {分|わ}ける: to divide; to separate — more general and everyday\n- {分離|ぶんり}する: to separate; to isolate — emphasizes detachment rather than partitioning\n- {分裂|ぶんれつ}する: to split; to break apart — often implies conflict or involuntary division",
